stormnic-igb
============

An original Rust implementation, licensed MIT (see LICENSE).

Acknowledgement: the hardware facts in src/igb.rs, src/ring.rs and
docs/hardware.md (register offsets, bit fields, the reset and queue-enable
sequences, the legacy descriptor formats) are from Intel's public
datasheets for the 82576, I350 and I210 Ethernet controllers. Two device
IDs (8086:1534, 8086:1535) that pci.ids lacks are from the device-ID list
of Intel's shared code as FreeBSD carries it (sys/dev/e1000/e1000_hw.h,
BSD-3-Clause); only the two numbers were taken.

No code was copied. Linux's igb and iPXE's intel.c (GPL) were not
translated. The UEFI glue (driver binding, SNP, console, PCI I/O, decode)
and the check app come from the siblings stormnic-realtek and
stormnic-virtio (MIT, same author).
